hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1410","From Muhammad bin Yahya, from Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle, he said: “The Messenger of God came out May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was among the people asking for water. He prayed two rak’ahs with them and recited the recitation aloud. He changed his robe, raised his hands, asked for water, and faced the Prophet. ""the qibla"""
